"executive_summary": "Words2Wheels is a novel framework designed to automatically generate customized driving policies for autonomous vehicles based on natural language user commands. Unlike existing methods that rely on predefined styles or data-driven inverse reinforcement learning (IRL) requiring specific historical data, Words2Wheels utilizes a Style-Customized Reward Function and a Driving Style Database. By leveraging Large Language Models (LLMs) and Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), the system retrieves, adapts, and generalizes driving styles to align with user preferences without needing prior driving data for the specific command. A Statistical Evaluation module ensures the generated policies match user intent by comparing metrics like speed and jerk against natural driving baselines. Experiments using the HighD dataset and human-in-the-loop evaluations demonstrate that Words2Wheels outperforms traditional models like the Intelligent Driver Model (IDM) in accuracy, generalization, and adaptability. The framework introduces a 'fuzzy memory' function to handle semantically similar commands, significantly enhancing user experience and interactivity in autonomous driving scenarios.",
